  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Four players draw one tile from the wall (stock) each turn and discard one face-up. Players may call chii (sequence from left neighbor's discard), pon (triplet from any discard), or kan (quad). Declare Riichi when one tile from tenpai (ready hand). Win by completing 14 tiles (4 melds and 1 pair) with at least one Yaku (scoring pattern), either by self-draw (tsumo) or on an opponent's discard (ron).",
    Player: "Four players draw one tile from the wall (stock) each turn and discard one face-up. Players may call chii (sequence from left neighbor's discard), pon (triplet from any discard), or kan (quad). Declare Riichi when one tile from tenpai (ready hand). Win by completing 14 tiles (4 melds and 1 pair) with at least one Yaku (scoring pattern), either by self-draw (tsumo) or on an opponent's discard (ron).",
    objective: "Complete a 14-tile hand with at least one 'Yaku' (scoring pattern).",
    gameplay: "Four players draw one tile from the wall (stock) each turn and discard one face-up. Players may call chii (sequence from left neighbor's discard), pon (triplet from any discard), or kan (quad). Declare Riichi when one tile from tenpai (ready hand). Win by completing 14 tiles (4 melds and 1 pair) with at least one Yaku (scoring pattern), either by self-draw (tsumo) or on an opponent's discard (ron).",
    keyRules: [
      'Each turn: draw one tile from the wall, then discard one face-up.',
      "Call chii (sequence) only from left neighbor; pon (triplet) and kan (quad) from any player's discard.",
      'Riichi: declare when one tile from tenpai; hand becomes closed for bonus.',
      'Win with 14 tiles (4 melds + 1 pair) and at least one Yaku.',
      'Furiten: if you could win on a discarded tile but did not call, you cannot win on discard until next turn.',
    ],
